<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <Description>Allocation-free numerical kernels (interpolation, discount-curve evaluation) and host-side optimisation and linear algebra: Levenberg-Marquardt, BFGS, Cholesky, symmetric eigen-decomposition, nearest correlation matrix.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    Allocation-free numerical kernels on plain doubles and arrays, shared by the host-side market model
    (InFine.QuantFinance.Market) and the kernel-side models (InFine.QuantFinance.Models). Methods here are written
    under the kernel rules (no allocation, no exceptions, no LINQ, no virtual calls) so that Hybridizer can transform
    them when a [Kernel] method calls them; Hybridizer follows explicit calls, so they need no attribute. This project
    must NOT reference Hybridizer: the market model depends on it and has to load on any host.
    Exception: the Levenberg-Marquardt least-squares solver (LevenbergMarquardt*.cs), the BFGS minimiser and finite
    differences (Bfgs.cs, FiniteDifferences.cs) and the dense linear algebra
    (Matrix, SymmetricEigen, Cholesky, NearestMatrix) are host-only code; they validate with exceptions and allocate
    freely, so never call them from a kernel.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>disable</ImplicitUsings>
    <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
    <RootNamespace>InFine.QuantFinance.Numerics</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
